<?xml version="1.0"?>
<system name="icing_alpha"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://jsbsim.sourceforge.net/JSBSimSystem.xsd">

<!-- ===================================================================
     Icing stall-onset shift (ADVANCEMENTS_BLUEPRINT section 1, work
     item P2; the stall-onset cue 14 CFR Part 60 FSTD Directive 2 asks
     for, as a STATED shift, not an accretion model).

     This file declares the one property. The sum

         icing/alpha-effective-rad = aero/alpha-rad + icing/alpha-shift-rad

     is NOT computed here: a <system> runs before FGAuxiliary in the
     JSBSim 1.2.4 schedule, so a system reading aero/alpha-rad sees the
     PREVIOUS step's alpha (measured: a system copy of alpha lags the
     property by 5.3e-4 .. 1.5e-3 rad over six steps of an elevator
     step, and the copy at neutral shift is therefore not bit-identical
     to alpha). core/control/derive.py instead injects the sum as a
     <function name="icing/alpha-effective-rad"> at the top of the
     airframe's <aerodynamics>, which FGAerodynamics evaluates before
     the axes with THIS step's alpha (measured: difference 0.0 at every
     step), and substitutes icing/alpha-effective-rad for aero/alpha-rad
     as the independent variable of the LIFT axis's alpha table.

     NEUTRAL VALUE: 0.0 (alpha + 0.0 == alpha to the last bit).

     NOT CLAIMED: only the LIFT table's alpha moves (drag, moment and
     the other axes keep the true alpha: a stated cue, not a physical
     model of an iced aerofoil); the shift is refused where the LIFT
     axis has no alpha-in-radians table or more than one.
     =================================================================== -->

  <property value="0.0">icing/alpha-shift-rad</property>

</system>
